  "summary": "Formal wood flooring pattern featuring elaborate geometric designs in wood veneers",
  "description": "Characterized by intricate geometric patterns using small pieces of wood veneer arranged in complex designs. Developed for Palace of Versailles to showcase craftsmanship and replace marble flooring.",
  "culturalContext": "Versailles parquet — the named-after-palace oak floor panel — interlaces squares, diagonals and quadrant fillets in one framed module, cut for Versailles' State Apartments (1678-84) to replace marble's cold with warm geometry under court ceremony. The pattern became \"the\" palace floor from Russian palaces to Manhattan co-ops; modern oak-engineering (Lauzon, Forbo) mass-produces it, and \"Versailles panel\" remains the luxury floor's most quoted geometry.",
